<title>JAPAN: Shin-Etsu U.S. unit may delay plant construction.</title>
<headline>Shin-Etsu U.S. unit may delay plant construction.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shin-Etsu Chemical Co Ltd said on Friday it may have to delay construction of a vinyl chloride plant in the United States, due to a delay in getting approval from the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA).</p>
<p>The delay is being caused by protests over the plan by the environmental group Greenpeace to the U.S. government, a Shin-Etsu spokesman said.</p>
<p>Shintech Inc, a wholly owned Shin-Etsu unit, announced in October 1996 that it would spend $700 million to build a second vinyl chloride plant in Louisiana, and planned to begin operations in mid-1998.</p>
</text>
